---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { projects } from "../../data/projects";

// Preserve the existing URL. Since 23 September 2026 the thesis studies modal language in preschool
// children, planned alongside an existing study; topic and design are still being agreed and no
// data exist. No collaborator or institution names (CONTEXT.md red line 6).
const project = projects.thesis;
---

<Base
  title={`${project.title} · Xiaochuan Li`}
  description="Master’s thesis in planning: how preschool children understand modal expressions, and how this relates to their reasoning about possibilities. No data have been collected."
  showProgress={true}
  toc={true}
>
  <article class="prose">
    <p class="!mb-6 !text-sm"><a href="/research" class="!text-[var(--color-accent)]">← Current Work</a></p>
    <div class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-[var(--color-text-dim)] font-medium mb-2">{project.status}</div>
    <h1>{project.title}</h1>
    <p class="text-[var(--color-text-muted)] italic !text-lg !mb-3">{project.question}</p>
    <p>{project.summary} {project.connection}</p>

    <h2>The connection to the formal analysis</h2>
    <p>
      <a href="/research/three-ways">Three Ways of Leaving <em>p</em> Unsettled</a> examines what
      possibility claims, explicit two-sided openness, and ignorance reports contribute to discourse.
      The thesis asks a developmental question about expressions of this kind: what preschool children
      understand when they hear them, and how that understanding relates to the way they reason about
      possibilities. The formal analysis suggests which contrasts are worth testing; it does not
      establish what children know.
    </p>

    <h2>A study with preschool children</h2>
    <p>
      Which expressions are compared, the age range, the materials, and the measures are still being
      agreed. If children’s performance on the language task is related to their reasoning in the
      existing study, that shows an association. It would not show that language drives the
      development of reasoning about possibilities.
    </p>

    <h2>Language models</h2>
    <p>
      The thesis includes no language-model study. Questions about what models can learn from
      linguistic input are pursued in separate projects.
    </p>

    <h2>Status</h2>
    <p class="cw-status">
      The thesis is being planned. No data have been collected, and there are no results.
    </p>
    <p class="!mt-10 !text-sm !text-[var(--color-text-dim)]"><a href="/research">← Back to Current Work</a></p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .cw-status { font-size: 0.98rem; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--color-text); padding: 1rem 1.2rem; border-left: 3px solid var(--color-accent); background: var(--color-surface); border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0; }
</style>
